{
  "title": "Stop repo-lock.sh from aborting when the lock is released mid-check",
  "description": "acquire_repo_lock in scripts/repo-lock.sh checks `[ -f \"$lock_dir/pid\" ]` and then reads it with `tr ... < \"$lock_dir/pid\"`. If the holder releases the lock between those two steps, the redirect fails with 'logs/locks/ui-deps.lock/pid: No such file or directory' and the waiter exits 1 instead of retrying mkdir. \
Seen as a flaky failure of tests/test_dependency_lock.py::test_concurrent_ui_dep_installs_take_turns during `make test` (passes when rerun alone). \
Read the pid with a guarded read (e.g. `lock_pid=$(tr -d '[:space:]' < \"$lock_dir/pid\" 2>/dev/null || true)`) so a vanished lock falls through to the next mkdir attempt.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "tooling",
    "flaky-test",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z",
}
